  "result": "Think of a restaurant.\n\nYou are the diner. You are the model. You cannot enter the kitchen. You can only read the menu and write on an order slip.\n\n- The **menu** lists what the kitchen can do. Each line says what the dish is. This is the tool description.\n- You write a **slip**: \"One soup, no salt.\" This is the tool call. It is only text. Writing it cooks nothing.\n- The **waiter** carries the slip to the kitchen. The waiter is your program. The waiter does the work, not you.\n- The **kitchen** makes the soup. The waiter brings the plate back.\n- You read the result. Then you write another slip, or you say \"I am done.\"\n\nEach time the plate arrives, you start a fresh look at the table: menu, your earlier slips, and the new plate.\n\nWhere it breaks: a real diner remembers the meal. A model only knows what is written on the table now.\n\nMakerspace example: you write \"check laser cutter, Friday\". The waiter looks at the calendar. The answer comes back as text.\n\nWant a short lesson with more examples and the details?\n\nQuick check: in this story, who actually cooks the soup?",
